{"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/arxiv/gr-qc/0511061?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/arxiv/gr-qc/0511061?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/arxiv/gr-qc/0511061?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/arxiv/gr-qc/0511061?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/arxiv/gr-qc/0511061?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/arxiv/gr-qc/0511061?format=cv"},"id":"gr-qc/0511061","uuid":"444deeef-69d5-403e-a216-6cfe81ee01cb","created":"2005-11-14T00:00:00+00:00","revision_id":92,"metadata":{"publication_info":[{"year":2006,"artid":"104031","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.D","journal_volume":"73"}],"citation_count":397,"report_numbers":[{"value":"CMU-TH-05-10"}],"citation_count_without_self_citations":350,"dois":[{"value":"10.1103/PhysRevD.73.104031"}],"titles":[{"title":"Post-Newtonian corrections to the motion of spinning bodies in NRGR"},{"title":"POSTNEWTONIAN"},{"title":"Post-Newtonian corrections to the motion of spinning bodies in NRGR","source":"arXiv"}],"$schema":"https://inspirehep.net/schemas/records/hep.json","authors":[{"uuid":"28090967-27fd-4d0f-9621-edc8ba3c8c91","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/992929"},"full_name":"Porto, Rafael A.","affiliations":[{"value":"Carnegie Mellon U.","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/902719"}}],"signature_block":"PARTr","curated_relation":true}],"curated":true,"texkeys":["Porto:2005ac"],"citeable":true,"keywords":[{"value":"11.27.+d","schema":"PACS"},{"value":"04.25.Nx","schema":"PACS"}],"refereed":true,"abstracts":[{"value":"In this paper we include spin and multipole moment effects in the formalism used to describe the motion of extended objects recently introduced in hep-th/0409156. A suitable description for spinning bodies is developed and spin-orbit, spin-spin and quadrupole-spin Hamiltonians are found at leading order. The existence of tidal, as well as self induced finite size effects is 